// cross_mod_float_param_value — v1.12 true scalar param kinds across
// modules. Pre-v1.12 the stub formal degraded to the RETURN kind (int),
// so `lib.fp(21)` passed 21's int bits into a float local (a denormal
// ~0) and the program exited 0 instead of 42. With the descriptor the
// argument widens int->float at the call site and the callee reads 21.0.
int fp(float x) {
    // float expression narrowed into an int return slot via `as`
    // (explicit-only since 0.7.5) — 21.0 * 2 truncates to 42.
    int r = (x * 2) as int;
    return r;
}
